and gather thy cattle, and all that thou hast in the field;
for upon every man and beast which shall be found in the field, and shall not be brought home, the hail shall come down upon them, and they shall die.

And Moses said unto him, As soon as I am gone out of the city, I will spread abroad my hands unto the LORD;
and the thunder shall cease, neither shall there be any more hail; that thou mayest know how that the earth
is the LORD’S.

Exodus 10.text:
And Moses stretched forth his rod over the land of Egypt, and the LORD brought an east wind upon the land all that day, and all
that night;
and when it was morning, the east wind brought the locusts.

Leviticus 13.text:
And the priest shall look on him the seventh day: and, behold,
if the plague in his sight be at a stay,
and the plague spread not in the skin; then the priest shall shut him up seven days more:

And in the seventh day the priest shall look on the plague: and, behold,
if the scall spread not, and there be in it no yellow hair, and the scall
be not in sight deeper than the skin;

And the man whose hair is fallen off his head, he
is bald;
yet is he clean.

Then the priest shall look upon it: and, behold,
if the rising of the sore
be white reddish in his bald head, or in his bald forehead, as the leprosy appeareth in the skin of the flesh;

The garment also that the plague of leprosy is in,
whether it be
 a woollen garment, or a linen garment;

Leviticus 14.text:
And if he
be poor, and cannot get so much; then he shall take one lamb
for a trespass offering to be waved, to make an atonement for him, and one tenth deal of fine flour mingled with oil for a meat offering, and a log of oil;

Leviticus 16.text:
Then shall he kill the goat of the sin offering, that
is
 for the people, and bring his blood within the vail, and do with that blood as he did with the blood of the bullock, and sprinkle it upon the mercy seat, and before the mercy seat:

